INT. ROOFTOP BOXING RING - BETWEEN ROUNDS - NIGHT

A ring bolted to a car-park roof. City glare behind the ropes. Wind flaps a banner.

DELROY "BLACKJACK" STANTON (30s, boxer) slumps on the stool, chest heaving, one eye swollen. ISAURA CAMPOS (50s, trainer, towel over her shoulder) crouches in front of him. BJÖRN HALVORSEN (60s, cutman, glove-stained thumbs) works on the eye.

ISAURA
Look at me.

BJÖRN
Hold still.

DELROY
I'm fine.

ISAURA
You're not fine. You're dropping the left.

BJÖRN
Don't talk. I've got a hole here.

DELROY
She keeps coming in under.

ISAURA
Then step back and counter. Step back.

BJÖRN
Chin up.

She slaps the water bottle into his hand. He rinses, spits into the bucket. Björn swabs. A bell rings. Delroy rises. Isaura pushes him into the ring.

ISAURA
Left hand, Jack!

BJÖRN
Go, go, go!

FADE OUT.
